WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:06.244
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Cambodia Grade nine English.

2
00:00:06.544 --> 00:00:10.418
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:10.718 --> 00:00:17.318
Unit eleven: Reported Speech. Today you will report what someone said without using their exact words.

4
00:00:17.618 --> 00:00:20.305
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:21.267 --> 00:00:24.151
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:25.017 --> 00:00:26.366
Reported speech.

7
00:00:27.350 --> 00:00:30.244
Reported speech means telling what someone said.

8
00:00:30.850 --> 00:00:33.082
Reported speech changes the tense.

9
00:00:33.683 --> 00:00:37.102
Your turn. Say: Reported speech.

10
00:00:39.967 --> 00:00:41.246
Reported speech.

11
00:00:41.983 --> 00:00:43.170
Direct speech.

12
00:00:44.183 --> 00:00:47.239
Direct speech means the exact words someone says.

13
00:00:47.850 --> 00:00:50.360
Direct speech uses quotation marks.

14
00:00:50.950 --> 00:00:54.357
Your turn. Say: Direct speech.

15
00:00:57.200 --> 00:00:58.515
Direct speech.

16
00:00:59.250 --> 00:01:00.054
Say.

17
00:01:01.050 --> 00:01:02.887
Say means to speak words.

18
00:01:03.483 --> 00:01:05.146
She said she was tired.

19
00:01:05.750 --> 00:01:07.984
Your turn. Say: Say.

20
00:01:10.833 --> 00:01:11.730
Say.

21
00:01:12.483 --> 00:01:13.148
Tell.

22
00:01:14.150 --> 00:01:16.115
Tell means to say something to someone.

23
00:01:16.717 --> 00:01:18.136
He told me a story.

24
00:01:18.750 --> 00:01:21.530
Your turn. Say: Tell.

25
00:01:24.367 --> 00:01:25.031
Tell.

26
00:01:25.783 --> 00:01:26.761
Ask.

27
00:01:27.750 --> 00:01:29.750
Ask means to request an answer.

28
00:01:30.350 --> 00:01:31.781
She asked where I lived.

29
00:01:32.383 --> 00:01:35.129
Your turn. Say: Ask.

30
00:01:37.967 --> 00:01:38.805
Ask.

31
00:01:39.550 --> 00:01:40.644
Backshift.

32
00:01:41.650 --> 00:01:44.439
Backshift means moving the tense one step back.

33
00:01:45.050 --> 00:01:47.084
Present becomes past in backshift.

34
00:01:47.683 --> 00:01:50.196
Your turn. Say: Backshift.

35
00:01:53.033 --> 00:01:54.011
Backshift.

36
00:01:54.750 --> 00:01:55.798
Yesterday.

37
00:01:56.783 --> 00:01:58.899
Yesterday means the day before today.

38
00:01:59.483 --> 00:02:01.645
He said he had come yesterday.

39
00:02:02.250 --> 00:02:04.368
Your turn. Say: Yesterday.

40
00:02:07.233 --> 00:02:08.281
Yesterday.

41
00:02:09.017 --> 00:02:10.064
The next day.

42
00:02:11.050 --> 00:02:13.096
The next day means the day after.

43
00:02:13.683 --> 00:02:15.567
She said she would come the next day.

44
00:02:16.183 --> 00:02:19.079
Your turn. Say: The next day.

45
00:02:21.933 --> 00:02:23.155
The next day.

46
00:02:23.967 --> 00:02:27.467
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:28.317 --> 00:02:32.220
Visal, how do we change direct speech into reported speech?

48
00:02:33.317 --> 00:02:44.493
We usually move the tense one step back. 'I am tired' becomes She said she was tired. We also change pronouns and time words, for example now becomes then.

49
00:02:45.583 --> 00:02:47.084
What about questions?

50
00:02:48.183 --> 00:03:00.834
In reported questions we use normal word order and no question mark. 'Where do you live?' becomes She asked me where I lived, and for yes-no questions we use if or whether.

51
00:03:01.950 --> 00:03:03.520
What do we do with commands?

52
00:03:04.617 --> 00:03:14.383
We use told plus an object plus to plus the base verb: 'Close the door' becomes He told me to close the door.

53
00:03:15.533 --> 00:03:16.999
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:17.850 --> 00:03:22.137
Grammar focus: Reported speech: backshift the tense.

55
00:03:22.437 --> 00:03:23.774
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:24.483 --> 00:03:27.632
'I am tired,' she said → She said she was tired.

57
00:03:28.517 --> 00:03:31.819
'Where do you live?' → She asked me where I lived.

58
00:03:32.767 --> 00:03:38.539
Move the tense back, change pronouns and time words, and use normal word order in reported questions.

59
00:03:39.283 --> 00:03:42.934
Be careful! Don't say: She said me she was tired.

60
00:03:44.900 --> 00:03:47.515
Say: She told me she was tired.

61
00:03:47.815 --> 00:03:49.211
Tell needs an object.

62
00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:52.501
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:53.300 --> 00:03:54.638
What the Teacher Said.

64
00:03:54.938 --> 00:03:57.448
The teacher said that the exam was on Friday.

65
00:03:58.433 --> 00:04:00.317
She told us to bring two pens.

66
00:04:01.333 --> 00:04:03.600
She asked whether we had finished the revision.

67
00:04:04.600 --> 00:04:07.087
Sokha said he had studied the night before.

68
00:04:08.100 --> 00:04:11.156
The teacher said she would give us more time the next day.

69
00:04:12.267 --> 00:04:16.094
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:16.950 --> 00:04:21.100
'I am tired,' she said. → She said she blank tired.

71
00:04:21.400 --> 00:04:24.508
A, is. B, has been. C, was.

72
00:04:28.067 --> 00:04:30.415
The answer is C: was.

73
00:04:31.550 --> 00:04:34.876
'Where do you live?' → She asked me where I blank.

74
00:04:35.176 --> 00:04:38.272
A, lived. B, do live. C, live you.

75
00:04:41.833 --> 00:04:43.601
The answer is A: lived.

76
00:04:44.750 --> 00:04:47.890
'Close the door.' → He told me blank the door.

77
00:04:48.190 --> 00:04:51.530
A, close. B, to close. C, closing.

78
00:04:55.067 --> 00:04:57.124
The answer is B: to close.

79
00:04:58.283 --> 00:05:00.457
What did the teacher tell the class to bring?

80
00:05:00.757 --> 00:05:04.538
A, a calculator. B, lunch. C, two pens.

81
00:05:08.100 --> 00:05:10.320
The answer is C: two pens.

82
00:05:11.483 --> 00:05:13.901
Now becomes blank in reported speech.

83
00:05:14.201 --> 00:05:17.471
A, then. B, today. C, yesterday.

84
00:05:21.033 --> 00:05:22.940
The answer is A: then.

85
00:05:24.133 --> 00:05:27.250
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:28.117 --> 00:05:30.128
Tell me something your teacher said today.

87
00:05:38.917 --> 00:05:40.359
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:40.659 --> 00:05:51.952
My teacher said that we would have a test next week. She told us to review the units and asked whether we had any questions. She also said that we should practise every day.

89
00:05:52.252 --> 00:05:54.019
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:05:54.917 --> 00:06:00.158
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and reported speech: backshift the tense.

91
00:06:00.458 --> 00:06:04.480
Today's value is communication. Speak clearly and listen carefully.

92
00:06:04.780 --> 00:06:07.270
See you in Unit twelve. Goodbye!

93
00:06:07.570 --> 00:06:10.826
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

